.\" Man page for Vuurmuur 0.8.2. Kept in sync with the option handling in
.\" vuurmuur_conf/vuurmuur_conf.c (optstring, prog_opts and
.\" print_commandline_args()).
.TH "VUURMUUR_CONF" "8" "February 2025" "Vuurmuur 0.8.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vuurmuur_conf \- ncurses GUI for administration of the Vuurmuur IPTables frontend.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vuurmuur_conf \fB[\-chdVW]\fR \fB[\-c\fR \fIconfig\-file\fR \fB][\-d\fR \fIdebug\-level\fR \fB]\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBvuurmuur_conf\fR
is the administration front end for Vuurmuur. It edits the zones, networks,
hosts, groups, services, interfaces, rules and block list, shows the status of
the firewall and lets the operator view the logs. Changes are written to the
backend (a text directory tree by default) and are only installed in the
kernel after \fBF11\fR (Apply changes), which tells
.BR vuurmuur (8)
and
.BR vuurmuur_log (8)
over shared memory to reload. That handshake is not a signal, and it waits for
both daemons to answer for up to 60 seconds.
.PP
The interface is a terminal application; it needs a terminal type ncurses
understands and it takes over the screen.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the possible command line options and exit.
.TP
\fB\-c\fR \fIfile\fR, \fB\-\-configfile\fR \fIfile\fR
Use \fIfile\fR as the Vuurmuur configuration file instead of the default.
.TP
\fB\-d\fR \fIlevel\fR, \fB\-\-debug\fR \fIlevel\fR
Enable debugging, 1 low, 3 high. Once the configuration is loaded the output
goes to the debug log file; the messages vuurmuur_conf emits before that point
go to stdout.
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print the version and exit.
.TP
\fB\-W\fR, \fB\-\-wizard\fR
Run the quick setup wizard instead of the GUI: it executes
.IR <datadir> /scripts/vuurmuur-wizard.sh
and exits. The wizard expects
.BR dialog (1)
on \s-1PATH\s0 and a group id of 0, and it fails its own self test unless a
basic configuration is already in place. The wizard's exit status is not
propagated: \fB\-W\fR exits 0 whether the script was missing, \fBdialog\fR was
not found, the wizard failed its self test, or the wizard was killed.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
0 on success, non zero on failure \- except for \fB\-W\fR, which exits 0 whatever
the wizard did, or whether it could be started at all.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/vuurmuur/vuurmuur_conf.conf
The GUI's own settings: which log files to show, logview buffer size, advanced
mode, background colour and the path to
.BR iptraf (8).
.TP
.I /etc/vuurmuur/config.conf
The shared Vuurmuur configuration, read to find the firewall binaries, the log
directory and the backend. The directory is fixed at build time unless
\fBVUURMUUR_SYSCONFDIR\fR is set; see ENVIRONMENT. See
.BR vuurmuur (8).
.TP
.I <datadir>/help/vuurmuur.hlp
The context sensitive help shown on \fBF12\fR. Which help file is used is chosen
from \fBLC_ALL\fR, \fBLC_CTYPE\fR or \fBLANG\fR, in that order, so a translated
install picks
.IR vuurmuur-<lang> .hlp
instead.
.TP
.I <logdir>/debug.log\fR, \fI<logdir>/error.log
Where \fB\-d\fR output and errors end up, \fI<logdir>\fR being the
.B LOGDIR
setting of the configuration file, \fI/var/log/vuurmuur\fR unless that setting
says otherwise.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VUURMUUR_SYSCONFDIR
Overrides the compiled-in configuration directory: the config file is then
.IR $VUURMUUR_SYSCONFDIR /vuurmuur/config.conf
and the textdir backend's object tree moves with it, because the backend finds
it through the configuration. A warning is logged whenever the variable is in
use. \fBLC_ALL\fR, \fBLC_CTYPE\fR and \fBLANG\fR select the help file, as
described under FILES.
.SH NOTES
vuurmuur_conf registers no signal handlers. If it is killed rather than quit,
the "configuration tool connected" flag in the daemons' shared memory table is
left as it was, because only the clean exit path sets it to the disconnected
value. The flag is rewritten when the GUI attaches again, so the effect does
not outlive one run.
.SH "REPORTING BUGS"
See https://www.vuurmuur.org/ for the project page and the current issue
tracker.
